# ansi — terminal color escape codes

## Reset

```sh
Color_Off='\e[0m'       # Text Reset
```

## Color code pattern

`\e[<style>;<color>m` — style 0=regular, 1=bold, 4=underline; colors 30-37 foreground, 40-47 background, 90-97 high intensity.

| Color  | FG | BG | HI FG | Bold FG |
| ------ | -- | -- | ----- | ------- |
| Black  | 30 | 40 | 90    | 1;30    |
| Red    | 31 | 41 | 91    | 1;31    |
| Green  | 32 | 42 | 92    | 1;32    |
| Yellow | 33 | 43 | 93    | 1;33    |
| Blue   | 34 | 44 | 94    | 1;34    |
| Purple | 35 | 45 | 95    | 1;35    |
| Cyan   | 36 | 46 | 96    | 1;36    |
| White  | 37 | 47 | 97    | 1;37    |

## Ready-to-source variable set

```sh
# Regular            Bold                  Underline             Background
Black='\e[0;30m';    BBlack='\e[1;30m';    UBlack='\e[4;30m';    On_Black='\e[40m'
Red='\e[0;31m';      BRed='\e[1;31m';      URed='\e[4;31m';      On_Red='\e[41m'
Green='\e[0;32m';    BGreen='\e[1;32m';    UGreen='\e[4;32m';    On_Green='\e[42m'
Yellow='\e[0;33m';   BYellow='\e[1;33m';   UYellow='\e[4;33m';   On_Yellow='\e[43m'
Blue='\e[0;34m';     BBlue='\e[1;34m';     UBlue='\e[4;34m';     On_Blue='\e[44m'
Purple='\e[0;35m';   BPurple='\e[1;35m';   UPurple='\e[4;35m';   On_Purple='\e[45m'
Cyan='\e[0;36m';     BCyan='\e[1;36m';     UCyan='\e[4;36m';     On_Cyan='\e[46m'
White='\e[0;37m';    BWhite='\e[1;37m';    UWhite='\e[4;37m';    On_White='\e[47m'
Color_Off='\e[0m'
```

## Real-world: service status in a homelab script

```sh
Green='\e[0;32m'; Red='\e[0;31m'; Color_Off='\e[0m'
if systemctl is-active --quiet plexmediaserver; then
    echo -e "${Green}Plex is up${Color_Off}"
else
    echo -e "${Red}Plex is DOWN${Color_Off}"
fi
```

## Real-world: colored warning banner

```sh
echo -e "\e[1;33;41m  PAY ATTENTION TO DETAILS IN ALL THINGS  \e[0m"
```

Remember `echo -e` (or `printf`) is required for `\e` to be interpreted.
